Date: 30 April 2026
Student: Data Science (Major Project Viva)
Project: OwnQuesta (https://ownquesta.com)
Deployment: AWS EC2 + AWS S3 + MongoDB Atlas
Tech Stack: React.js + Next.js (Frontend), Node.js + Express (Backend), FastAPI (AI/Lab services)

====================================================================
1) 30-SECOND INTRO (VERY IMPORTANT)
====================================================================
Use this exact simple intro in viva:

"Good morning sir/ma'am. My project name is OwnQuesta. It is an AI-powered learning and AutoML platform for students. Users can upload datasets, run guided analysis, and generate outputs like model scripts. The frontend is built with React.js and Next.js. The backend API is built with Node.js and Express with MongoDB Atlas for data storage. For AI and code-execution workflows, I integrated FastAPI services and agent-based flow using OpenAI and Anthropic APIs. The platform is deployed on AWS using EC2 and S3."

Short backup version:
"OwnQuesta is an AI-enabled educational AutoML platform. I used Next.js in frontend, Node.js in backend, FastAPI for agent/lab services, and deployed on AWS with MongoDB Atlas."

====================================================================
2) 2-MINUTE PROJECT EXPLANATION (SPEAKABLE SCRIPT)
====================================================================
"The problem I targeted is that many students in data science struggle to move from theory to practical implementation. They may know concepts, but they get blocked in coding, model training flow, and deployment understanding.

OwnQuesta solves this by combining a web learning platform and AI-assisted lab workflow. Users can register/login, access dashboard features, upload dataset files, and use AutoML/lab modules. The system guides users through steps and generates meaningful outputs.

From architecture side, I separated concerns into:
1. Frontend layer using Next.js and React.
2. Core backend APIs using Node.js and Express.
3. AI/lab microservices using FastAPI.

I used MongoDB Atlas as cloud database. Deployment is on AWS EC2, and S3 is used for static or file storage needs.

Technically, this is useful because each layer is independently scalable. Next.js gives modern UI and routing. Node.js handles authentication and main business APIs. FastAPI handles Python-based AI execution tasks, sessionized code execution, and integration with OpenAI/Anthropic for agentic workflows.

So the project combines web engineering, backend APIs, cloud deployment, and data science workflow support in one complete product."

