4) SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE EXPLANATION (HOW TO SPEAK)
====================================================================
"I followed a multi-service architecture. Frontend is a Next.js app. Core business APIs are in Node.js Express backend. AI and code-execution components are in FastAPI services because Python ecosystem is better for ML-oriented tasks. This separation helps maintainability and scaling. If AI traffic increases, I can scale FastAPI service separately without impacting user-auth APIs."

One-line technical highlight:
"I used the right language for the right layer: JavaScript stack for web workflows and Python stack for AI workflows."

====================================================================
5) REACT.JS EXPLANATION (VIVA FRIENDLY)
====================================================================
What is React?
- React is a component-based JavaScript library for building interactive UIs.

Why React in your project?
- Reusable components reduced duplication.
- State-driven rendering made dashboard and dynamic screens easy.
- Strong ecosystem and compatibility with Next.js.

Concepts you can say confidently:
- Component-based architecture
- State and props
- Conditional rendering
- Event handling
- Reusability and maintainability

Sample viva answer:
"I used React because OwnQuesta has many dynamic UI parts like dashboard views, workflow steps, and user-specific content. React components helped me keep the UI modular and maintainable."

====================================================================
6) NEXT.JS EXPLANATION (VIVA FRIENDLY)
====================================================================
What is Next.js?
- Next.js is a React framework for production-grade apps with routing, rendering strategies, and backend utilities.

Why Next.js for OwnQuesta?
- File-based routing made app structure clean.
- Better performance options like SSR/SSG when required.
- API route support in frontend project where needed.
- Good developer experience and scalable structure.

Concepts to mention:
- App Router structure (app directory)
- Server/client component separation (conceptually)
- Routing and nested pages
- Optimized build/deployment flow

Sample viva answer:
"I selected Next.js because it gives me React flexibility plus production features like routing, optimization, and better structure for larger applications."

====================================================================
7) NODE.JS + EXPRESS EXPLANATION
====================================================================
What is Node.js?
- Node.js runs JavaScript on server side with event-driven, non-blocking I/O.

Why Node.js in your project?
- Same language across frontend and backend reduces context switching.
- Fast API development for auth, user, admin, and workflow endpoints.
- Easy integration with MongoDB and modern npm ecosystem.

What Express adds:
- Routing and middleware structure
- Clean REST API implementation
- Easy request/response handling

Viva answer:
"Node.js with Express allowed me to quickly build scalable REST APIs for authentication, user data, admin operations, and platform workflows."

====================================================================
8) FASTAPI EXPLANATION (VERY IMPORTANT FOR DATA SCIENCE PROFILE)
====================================================================
What is FastAPI?
- FastAPI is a high-performance Python web framework for building APIs, especially good for data and AI services.

Why FastAPI in OwnQuesta?
- Python ecosystem is strongest for data science and ML tasks.
- Easy to create typed APIs and structured request models.
- Good performance for microservice endpoints.
- Works well for AI-agent orchestration and execution services.

Project-specific points you can say:
- Session creation endpoint for execution lifecycle.
- Execute endpoint for code execution with timeout and restrictions.
- Upload endpoint for CSV/Excel datasets.
- Health endpoint for service monitoring.
- CORS enabled for frontend integration.

Strong viva line:
"I used FastAPI because my AI/lab workflows are Python-centric, and FastAPI gives fast, typed, and production-friendly APIs for those tasks."

====================================================================
9) DATABASE + CLOUD EXPLANATION
====================================================================
MongoDB Atlas:
- Cloud-hosted NoSQL database
- Flexible document schema for user/project/activity data
- Easy scaling and managed operations

AWS EC2:
- Hosts application services
- Full control over deployment environment

AWS S3:
- Used for object/static/file storage use-cases
- Durable and scalable storage layer

Viva-ready answer:
"I used MongoDB Atlas for managed cloud database, EC2 for compute hosting, and S3 for scalable storage. This gives production-like deployment instead of only local development."

